  "notes": "{連|つら}なる is an intransitive godan verb. The transitive counterpart is {連|つら}ねる (to line up, to take along).\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{連|つら}なっている describes a continuous state of being lined up or extending in a row. This is the most common form.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～が{連|つら}なる (something stretches in a row)\n- ～に{連|つら}なる (to attend/join something)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {山|やま}が{連|つら}なる (mountains stretch in a row)\n- {山脈|さんみゃく}が{連|つら}なる (a mountain range extends)\n- {席|せき}に{連|つら}なる (to attend a gathering)\n- {名|な}を{連|つら}ねる (to have one's name listed — transitive form)",
